    "source": "1810 census projected to 1812, free adult men outside the Southern states; the census gives free white males in bands (16\u201326, 26\u201345, 45+), so men 21+ are split from the 16\u201326 band. Voters were men meeting each state's rules: many states still required property or taxpaying qualifications (Virginia and Rhode Island a freehold; Maryland dropped its test in 1810). Electors were chosen by popular vote in 9 states; elsewhere (Connecticut, Delaware, Georgia, Louisiana, New Jersey, New York, North Carolina, South Carolina and Vermont) men cast no presidential vote. Free Black men could vote in some Northern states on the same or stricter terms."
   },
